🔍 SEND_CHAT_MESSAGE: Получены данные: {'message': '/add', 'session_id': 38, 'parsed_file_data': {'id': 104376159, 'url': 'https://store.huntflow.ru/uploads3/named/e/2/9/e295ad6f432befb4abfc62a62cca7915.pdf/CV_Aliaksei_Charniauski.pdf?s=Ss7yZfajh5Sa9fwIpyq-bA&e=1768963520', 'content_type': 'application/pdf', 'name': 'CV_Aliaksei_Charniauski.pdf', 'text': 'ALIAKSEI CHARNIAUSKI\nSoftware Engineer | Frontend Developer\n\n+375(29)645-23-35 charniauski.aliaksei@gmail.com https://www.linkedin.com/in/acharniauski Belarus\n\nSUMMARY\n\nFrontend Software Engineer specializing in React, Angular, and TypeScript, with extensive \nexperience in single-page applications (SPAs) across Fintech, Geo/Mapping, EdTech, and \nSaaS/B2B platforms.\nSkilled in building data-intensive, high-performance, and maintainable web interfaces, \nleveraging modern frontend frameworks, state management, and UI libraries.\nExperienced in microfrontend architectures, dashboard development, and complex data-\ndriven interfaces, delivering scalable solutions for enterprise-level applications.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nFrontend Developer 09/2025 - Present\xa0 Belarus\nGeo-analytics Web Platform with microfrontend architecture\n\nSPA development using React 19 and TypeScript, with Redux Toolkit for state \nmanagement and Rspack / Rsbuild for bundling.\nImplementation of interactive maps and geospatial visualizations using MapLibre GL; work \nwith geospatial data and computations (Turf.js, rbush, proj4).\nData and analytics visualization using Chart.js and custom UI components.\nDesign of a shared host application and isolated feature modules, including \nmicrofrontends with independent loading, build, and deployment processes (Module \nFederation).\nBackend integration via OpenAPI specifications.\nDevelopment of high-performance UI components for rendering large volumes of data.\n\nFrontend Developer\nHES FinTech 02/2025 - 09/2025\xa0 Belarus\nFintech Backoffice platform for Financial and Credit Data Management\n\nSPA development using React 18, TypeScript, MobX, and Vite.\nUI implementation based on Ant Design, including complex forms and data-heavy tables.\nBackend integration via a typed API client (axios, autogenerated client).\nLocalization setup and dynamic translation loading using i18next.\nUI components development and documentation using Storybook.\n\nBorrower Portal & Backoffice Platform for a Fintech Lending System\nSPA development using React 17, TypeScript, and MobX.\nImplementation of complex multi-step forms and questionnaires with Form.io.\nDocument upload and preview interfaces using PDF.js and react-doc-viewer.\nUI development using Ant Design, Bootstrap, and styled-components.\n\nSoftware Engineer\nSofteq 10/2021 - 01/2025\xa0 Poland\n\nImplement component-based architectures using React/Angular and related stacks.\nDesign and implement user interfaces and layouts based on mockups and wireframes.\nClosely collaborate with backend developers, QA engineers, and other team members to \nensure a consistent and efficient development process.\nConduct code reviews to ensure adherence to coding standards, best practices, and \nproject guidelines.\nRefactor existing code to enhance readability, maintainability, and performance.\nTroubleshoot and resolve bugs reported by users or identified through testing.\nGather and analyze customer feedback to identify areas for improvement and feature \nrequests.\nDeliver Customer Care department services: provide full guidance and assist customers in \ntroubleshooting and resolving technical issues related to products or services.\n\nKEY ACHIEVEMENTS\n\nSoftware Engineer and Frontend Developer roles\n• Designed and implemented the user interface for 7 web applications and managed the \nmaintenance of 9 projects across diverse tech stacks.\n• Frontend performance optimizations (rendering, memoization, virtualization) applied to \ndata-heavy views, reducing initial render time by ~30%.\n• Optimization of map rendering and layer updates in MapLibre, improving FPS stability by \n~35% on large geospatial datasets.\n• Proactively resolved 20+ potential user issues before they were reported, leading to about \n20% decrease in support tickets.\n• Refactored legacy code, reducing technical debt by 15% and improving maintainability.\n• Conducted over 200 code reviews, ensuring adherence to coding standards and improving \ncode quality.\n• Handled over 50 customer support cases, achieving a 95% satisfaction rate.\n\nSKILLS\n\nJavaScript TypeScript React\n\nRedux / Redux Toolkit MobX Angular\n\nRxJS HTML CSS / SCSS\n\nMaterial UI / Ant Design / MUI Git\n\nChart.js MapLibre Form.io Next.js\n\nGitHub / GitLab / Bitbucket Vite\n\nREST API OpenAPI Rsbuild / Rspack\n\nModule Federation Code Review\n\nProject Management Business Analysis\n\nSoftware Testing / QA\n\nLANGUAGES\n\nEnglish Proficient\n\nSTRENGTHS\n\nRapid learning and adaptability\nProven ability to quickly master new technologies \nand work across diverse tech stacks.\n\nFull software development lificycle \nunderstanding\nProject management background, combined with \nsoftware testing and business analysis training, \nprovides a holistic view of the development \nprocess.\n\nEfficient collaboration\nAbility to build effective collaboration with all \nproject stakeholders - engineers, QA, analysts, \ndesigners, and managers - to deliver high-quality \nresults.\n\nPROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT\n\nTRAINING / COURSES\n\nReact - The Complete Guide (Udemy.com)\nAngular - The Complete Guide (Udemy.com)\nModern HTML and CSS (learn.javascript.ru)\nBusiness Analysis (IT Academy)\nSoftware Testing Introduction (EPAM UpSkill)\n\nwww.enhancv.com \u200bPowered by\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n•\n\n•\n•\n\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n\n•\n•\n•\n•\n\n•\n•\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n•\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n\n\u200b \u200b \u200b \u200b\n\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/acharniauski\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/acharniauski\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/acharniauski\nhttps://enhancv.com/resume\nhttps:/